# DESK33 -- F7 launches the application bound to it.
#
# The card is method/seed_d33.sh's image: C:\NEWDESK.INF carries
# `#G 06 FF C:\ARGVTEST.NAP@ *.XYZ@ 107 @`, i.e. `a_funkey = 7` on
# C:\ARGVTEST.NAP.  Until DESK33 `check_function_key` recognised the key and
# then fell through -- `process_funkey` (deskmain.c:1087-1106) did not exist,
# so nothing started.
#
# The pointer is PARKED at the bottom right for the whole run: nothing is
# clicked, the only input is the key.  F7 is IKBD scancode 0x41 (make) / 0xC1
# (break) -- scancode.h FUNKEY_01 = 0x3B00, so F7 = 0x3B + 6.
#
#   B_IDLE   the desktop, nothing selected
#   C_F7     after F7: ARGVTEST ran (it prints its argc/argv to the console and
#            terminates by itself), the desktop is back
#
# The proof is in the serial log, not on the picture: `[d33] process_funkey(7)
# -> C:\ARGVTEST.NAP` followed by the program's own `ARGVTEST:` lines.
100 parkbr
300 move 600 240
1000 arm
1200 mark A_IDLE
1600 parkbr
2400 mark B_IDLE
3000 key 41
3010 key c1
6000 mark C_F7
# -- F6 (scancode 0x40) is bound to nothing: `process_funkey` finds no ANODE
#    and returns -1, so `hndl_kbd` falls through to the rest of its chain and
#    the desktop is unchanged.
7000 key 40
7010 key c0
9000 mark D_F6
